      <Comment source="pmngroup">An &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; mutant (&lt;i&gt;pgi1-1&lt;/i&gt;) with a missense mutation of the &lt;i&gt;PGI1&lt;/i&gt; gene has a reduced plastidic phosphoglucose isomerase (PGI) activity representing only 6.5% of that of the wild-type |CITS:[10806248]|. The mutant is deficient in starch synthesis.</Comment>
